Q5: If the mutation is a nucleotide substitution, is it synonymous, missense or nonsense?
The mutation is a nucleotide substitution. Since it changes the encoded amino acid (Ile → Thr), it is a missense mutation 
(not synonymous, since the amino acid changes, and not nonsense, since no stop codon is created).
Q6: If nucleotides have been inserted or deleted, could the change alter the reading frame (i.e. frameshift)?
A frameshift occurs when the number of inserted or deleted nucleotides is not a multiple of three. In our case there are 
no insertions or deletions (no gaps in the alignment), so the reading frame is not altered and there is no frameshift.
